although sony and marvel studios have  shared custody of tom holland spider-man  so that he can exist in the marvel  cinematic universe alongside the  avengers the former studio is still  pushing ahead with its own universe of  spidey villains and anti-heroes venom  was a surprise hit back in 2018 raking  in 856 million dollars so audiences are  clearly interested in sony's edgy  approach to superheroes it's no surprise  then that the studio is working on a  solo craven the hunter film starring  aaron taylor johnson as well as a madame  web adventure with dakota johnson and  sydney sweeney meanwhile jared leto's  morbius is finally set to arrive in  theaters on april 1st and it's been a  long time coming the movie was  originally intended to debut on july 10  2020 but that was delayed almost  immediately and then the pandemic hit  causing sony to push the release back  several more times morbius follows letto  as dr michael morbius a genius who is  determined to find a cure for the rare  blood disorder that he suffered from  since childhood his research leads him  to an experimental procedure using bats  and it transforms him into a vicious  beast with a comic accurate gray skin  and red eyes enhanced senses super  strength and the ability to fly  unfortunately he also has to contend  with matt smith's luxurious crown and  fbi agent simon stroud played by tyrese  gibson the first reactions from critics  have made their way online and they  paint an interesting picture of sony's  latest marvel movie collider contributor  sab astley blasted the movie for its  poor story tweeting mobius is about as  bad as you were expecting a 2005 plot  collides with visually confusing cgi to  create a bit of a snooze fest but don't  worry they've saved the worst for last  featuring some of the worst post-credits  scenes you've ever seen  sony are off their rocker the we have a  hulk podcast nicola austin echoed the  sentiment noting that it doesn't live up  to the venom corner of sony's marvel  universe she posted well morbius is  unfortunately not great some really  shoddy vfx and 2000s formulaic plot and  definitely not as fun as venom really  confused at the future of the sony  spiderverse following the post credits  scenes and the editing meanwhile escape  film club tweeted that the film's  visuals can't save it posting morbius  proves that no matter how many famous  faces or shiny visuals you squeeze in  sony will always find a way to  impressively misunderstand the basic  storytelling film critic renviera  followed that up writing matt smith  gloriously hams up the place and oliver  wood delivers some visual flair to the  action sequences aside from that the bad  plotting and messy cgi confusing editing  and worse sound mix result in absolute  incoherence but the post credits managed  to outdo it all one of the biggest  questions fans have about morbius is  when is he going to meet the other sony  marvel characters like venom obviously  an earlier trailer reveals a look at  michael keaton's vulture which implies  that a sinister 6 style team-up is on  the way at some point sony has been keen  to make a movie about the squad of  spider-man villains for quite some time  and the original plan was to spin it out  of the amazing spider-man franchise for  the moment it's not clear if or when  morbius will cross over with the likes  of venom vulture or craven although  jared leto previously told screen rants  that all of the marvel characters the  living vampire could meet quote venom  would make a lot of sense that would be  fun it's worth pointing out that just  because the film has had a negative  reaction from critics doesn't mean it  won't be successful at the box office at  the end of the day if morbius is hugely  profitable then sony will likely  continue to use the character in sequels  and crossovers letto himself revealed on  the late late show with james corden  that he could easily cross over into the  upcoming blade movie for now it's  probably best to go into morbius with a  little caution  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

